  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 1218 PM CST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nRains will continue in our east 1/2 into Sunday morning, with a\ncontinuation of the forcing and moisture exiting our east by \nmid afternoon. Highs Sunday will be rather challenging with \nincreasing CAA and cloud cover, though a mild start to the day.\nAt this time, mainly 45-50 is expected in the west, with lower \nto upper 50s in the central and eastern counties. If the front \nslows or speeds up at all, these are subject to considerable \nchange. Either day, a cloudy, damp, blustery day will develop by\nmid morning in all areas, and a return to \"normal\" November \nweather is on it's way. \n\nHigh pressure will build into the region Sunday night and Monday, \nwith decreasing winds, which will remain north to northwest, likely \naround 10 mph between 6 AM and 4 PM Monday, in all counties. \n\nCool Canadian high pressure will remain over the region through mid \nweek, resulting in persistently cool /seasonal weather with dry \nconditions and relatively light winds.",
